 "durationMinutes": 44,
 "reviewStatus": "UNREVIEWED",
 "translations": [
  {
   "key": "en-translation",
   "lang": "en",
   "variant": "translation",
   "translator": "Adam Pearcey, 2006 (revised)",
   "sourceName": "Lotsawa House - The Thirty-Seven Practices of All the Bodhisattvas",
   "sourceUrl": "https://www.lotsawahouse.org/tibetan-masters/gyalse-thogme-zangpo/37-practices-all-bodhisattvas",
   "license": "CC-BY-NC-4.0",
   "licenseNote": "Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International; as stated on Lotsawa House",
   "note": "Stanza numbers moved into the section field.",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Namo Lokeśvarāya!"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "You see that all things are beyond coming and going,"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "Yet still you strive solely for the sake of living beings—"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "To you, my precious guru inseparable from Lord Avalokita,"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "I offer perpetual homage, respectfully, with body, speech and mind."
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "The perfect buddhas, who are the source of all benefit and joy,"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "Come into being through accomplishing the sacred Dharma."
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "And since this in turn depends on knowing how to practise,"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "I shall now describe the practices of all the buddhas’ heirs."
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to study, reflect and meditate,",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "Tirelessly, both day and night, without ever straying into idleness,",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 12,
     "text": "In order to free oneself and others from this ocean of saṃsāra,",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "Having gained this supreme vessel—a free, well-favoured human life, so difficult to find.",
     "section": "Verse 1"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to leave behind one’s homeland,",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "Where our attachment to family and friends overwhelms us like a torrent,",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "While our aversion towards enemies rages inside us like a blazing fire,",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "And delusion’s darkness obscures what must be adopted and abandoned.",
     "section": "Verse 2"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to take to solitary places,",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "Avoiding the unwholesome, so that destructive emotions gradually fade away,",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "And, in the absence of distraction, virtuous practice naturally gains strength;",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "Whilst, with awareness clearly focused, we gain conviction in the teachings.",
     "section": "Verse 3"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to renounce this life’s concerns,",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "For friends and relatives, long acquainted, must all go their separate ways;",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "Wealth and prized possessions, painstakingly acquired, must all be left behind;",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "And consciousness, the guest who lodges in the body, must in time depart.",
     "section": "Verse 4"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to avoid destructive friends,",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "In whose company the three poisons of the mind grow stronger,",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "And we engage less and less in study, reflection and meditation,",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "So that love and compassion fade away until they are no more.",
     "section": "Verse 5"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to cherish spiritual friends,",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "By regarding them as even more precious than one’s own body,",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "Since they are the ones who will help to rid us of all our faults,",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 33,
     "text": "And make our virtues grow ever greater just like the waxing moon.",
     "section": "Verse 6"
    },
    {
     "n": 34,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to take refuge in the Three Jewels,",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 35,
     "text": "Since they will never fail to provide protection for all who call upon them,",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 36,
     "text": "For whom are the ordinary gods of this world ever capable of helping,",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 37,
     "text": "As long as they themselves are trapped within saṃsāra’s vicious cycle?",
     "section": "Verse 7"
    },
    {
     "n": 38,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is never to commit a harmful act,",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 39,
     "text": "Even though not to do so might put one’s very life at risk,",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 40,
     "text": "For the Sage himself has taught how negative actions will ripen",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 41,
     "text": "Into the manifold miseries of the lower realms, so difficult to endure.",
     "section": "Verse 8"
    },
    {
     "n": 42,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to strive towards the goal,",
     "section": "Verse 9"
    },
    {
     "n": 43,
     "text": "Which is the supreme state of changeless, everlasting liberation,",
     "section": "Verse 9"
    },
    {
     "n": 44,
     "text": "Since all the happiness of the three realms lasts but a moment,",
     "section": "Verse 9"
    },
    {
     "n": 45,
     "text": "And then is quickly gone, just like dewdrops on blades of grass.",
     "section": "Verse 9"
    },
    {
     "n": 46,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to arouse bodhicitta,",
     "section": "Verse 10"
    },
    {
     "n": 47,
     "text": "So as to bring freedom to all sentient beings, infinite in number.",
     "section": "Verse 10"
    },
    {
     "n": 48,
     "text": "For how can true happiness ever be found while our mothers,",
     "section": "Verse 10"
    },
    {
     "n": 49,
     "text": "Who have cared for us throughout the ages, endure such pain?",
     "section": "Verse 10"
    },
    {
     "n": 50,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to make a genuine exchange",
     "section": "Verse 11"
    },
    {
     "n": 51,
     "text": "Of one’s own happiness and well-being for all the sufferings of others.",
     "section": "Verse 11"
    },
    {
     "n": 52,
     "text": "Since all misery comes from seeking happiness for oneself alone,",
     "section": "Verse 11"
    },
    {
     "n": 53,
     "text": "Whilst perfect buddhahood is born from the wish for others’ good.",
     "section": "Verse 11"
    },
    {
     "n": 54,
     "text": "Even if others, in the grips of great desire, should steal,",
     "section": "Verse 12"
    },
    {
     "n": 55,
     "text": "Or encourage others to take away, all the wealth that I possess,",
     "section": "Verse 12"
    },
    {
     "n": 56,
     "text": "To dedicate to them entirely my body, possessions and all my merits",
     "section": "Verse 12"
    },
    {
     "n": 57,
     "text": "From the past, present and future— this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 12"
    },
    {
     "n": 58,
     "text": "Even if others should seek to cut off my head,",
     "section": "Verse 13"
    },
    {
     "n": 59,
     "text": "Though I’ve done them not the slightest wrong,",
     "section": "Verse 13"
    },
    {
     "n": 60,
     "text": "To take upon myself, out of compassion,",
     "section": "Verse 13"
    },
    {
     "n": 61,
     "text": "All the harms they have amassed—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 13"
    },
    {
     "n": 62,
     "text": "Even if others should declare before the world",
     "section": "Verse 14"
    },
    {
     "n": 63,
     "text": "All manner of unpleasant things about me,",
     "section": "Verse 14"
    },
    {
     "n": 64,
     "text": "To speak only of their qualities in return,",
     "section": "Verse 14"
    },
    {
     "n": 65,
     "text": "With a mind that’s filled with love—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 14"
    },
    {
     "n": 66,
     "text": "Even if others should expose my hidden faults or deride me",
     "section": "Verse 15"
    },
    {
     "n": 67,
     "text": "When speaking amidst great gatherings of many people,",
     "section": "Verse 15"
    },
    {
     "n": 68,
     "text": "To conceive of them as spiritual friends and to bow",
     "section": "Verse 15"
    },
    {
     "n": 69,
     "text": "Before them in respect—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 15"
    },
    {
     "n": 70,
     "text": "Even if others whom I have cared for like children of my own",
     "section": "Verse 16"
    },
    {
     "n": 71,
     "text": "Should turn upon me and treat me as an enemy,",
     "section": "Verse 16"
    },
    {
     "n": 72,
     "text": "To regard them only with special fondness and affection,",
     "section": "Verse 16"
    },
    {
     "n": 73,
     "text": "As a mother would her ailing child—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 16"
    },
    {
     "n": 74,
     "text": "Even if others, equal or inferior to me in status,",
     "section": "Verse 17"
    },
    {
     "n": 75,
     "text": "Should, out of arrogance, disparage me,",
     "section": "Verse 17"
    },
    {
     "n": 76,
     "text": "To honour them, as I would my teacher,",
     "section": "Verse 17"
    },
    {
     "n": 77,
     "text": "By bowing down my head before them—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 17"
    },
    {
     "n": 78,
     "text": "Even though I may be destitute and despised by all,",
     "section": "Verse 18"
    },
    {
     "n": 79,
     "text": "Beset with terrible illness and plagued by evil spirits,",
     "section": "Verse 18"
    },
    {
     "n": 80,
     "text": "Still to take upon myself all beings’ ills and harmful actions,",
     "section": "Verse 18"
    },
    {
     "n": 81,
     "text": "Without ever losing heart—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 18"
    },
    {
     "n": 82,
     "text": "Even though I may be famous and revered by all,",
     "section": "Verse 19"
    },
    {
     "n": 83,
     "text": "And as rich as Vaiśravaṇa, the god of wealth himself,",
     "section": "Verse 19"
    },
    {
     "n": 84,
     "text": "To see the futility of all the glory and riches of this world",
     "section": "Verse 19"
    },
    {
     "n": 85,
     "text": "And to remain without conceit—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 19"
    },
    {
     "n": 86,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to subdue the mind",
     "section": "Verse 20"
    },
    {
     "n": 87,
     "text": "With the forces of loving kindness and compassion.",
     "section": "Verse 20"
    },
    {
     "n": 88,
     "text": "For unless the real adversary—my own anger—is defeated,",
     "section": "Verse 20"
    },
    {
     "n": 89,
     "text": "Outer enemies, though I may conquer them, will continue to appear.",
     "section": "Verse 20"
    },
    {
     "n": 90,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to turn away immediately",
     "section": "Verse 21"
    },
    {
     "n": 91,
     "text": "From those things which bring desire and attachment.",
     "section": "Verse 21"
    },
    {
     "n": 92,
     "text": "For the pleasures of the senses are just like salty water:",
     "section": "Verse 21"
    },
    {
     "n": 93,
     "text": "The more we taste of them, the more our thirst increases.",
     "section": "Verse 21"
    },
    {
     "n": 94,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is never to entertain concepts,",
     "section": "Verse 22"
    },
    {
     "n": 95,
     "text": "Which revolve around dualistic notions of perceiver and perceived,",
     "section": "Verse 22"
    },
    {
     "n": 96,
     "text": "In the knowledge that all these appearances are but the mind itself,",
     "section": "Verse 22"
    },
    {
     "n": 97,
     "text": "Whilst mind’s own nature is forever beyond the limitations of ideas.",
     "section": "Verse 22"
    },
    {
     "n": 98,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to let go of grasping",
     "section": "Verse 23"
    },
    {
     "n": 99,
     "text": "When encountering things one finds pleasant or attractive,",
     "section": "Verse 23"
    },
    {
     "n": 100,
     "text": "Considering them to be like rainbows in the summer skies—",
     "section": "Verse 23"
    },
    {
     "n": 101,
     "text": "Beautiful in appearance, yet in truth devoid of any substance.",
     "section": "Verse 23"
    },
    {
     "n": 102,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to recognize delusion",
     "section": "Verse 24"
    },
    {
     "n": 103,
     "text": "Whenever one is confronted by adversity or misfortune.",
     "section": "Verse 24"
    },
    {
     "n": 104,
     "text": "For these sufferings are just like the death of a child in a dream,",
     "section": "Verse 24"
    },
    {
     "n": 105,
     "text": "And it’s so exhausting to cling to delusory perceptions as real.",
     "section": "Verse 24"
    },
    {
     "n": 106,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to give out of generosity,",
     "section": "Verse 25"
    },
    {
     "n": 107,
     "text": "With no hopes of karmic recompense or expectation of reward.",
     "section": "Verse 25"
    },
    {
     "n": 108,
     "text": "For if those who seek awakening must give even their own bodies,",
     "section": "Verse 25"
    },
    {
     "n": 109,
     "text": "What need is there to mention mere outer objects and possessions?",
     "section": "Verse 25"
    },
    {
     "n": 110,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to observe ethical restraint,",
     "section": "Verse 26"
    },
    {
     "n": 111,
     "text": "Without the slightest intention of continuing in saṃsāric existence.",
     "section": "Verse 26"
    },
    {
     "n": 112,
     "text": "For lacking discipline one will never secure even one’s own well-being,",
     "section": "Verse 26"
    },
    {
     "n": 113,
     "text": "And so any thought of bringing benefit to others would be absurd.",
     "section": "Verse 26"
    },
    {
     "n": 114,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to cultivate patience,",
     "section": "Verse 27"
    },
    {
     "n": 115,
     "text": "Free from any trace of animosity towards anyone at all,",
     "section": "Verse 27"
    },
    {
     "n": 116,
     "text": "Since any potential source of harm is like a priceless treasure",
     "section": "Verse 27"
    },
    {
     "n": 117,
     "text": "To the bodhisattva who is eager to enjoy a wealth of virtue.",
     "section": "Verse 27"
    },
    {
     "n": 118,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to strive with enthusiastic diligence—",
     "section": "Verse 28"
    },
    {
     "n": 119,
     "text": "The source of all good qualities—when working for the sake of all who live;",
     "section": "Verse 28"
    },
    {
     "n": 120,
     "text": "Seeing that even śrāvakas and pratyekabuddhas, who labour for themselves alone,",
     "section": "Verse 28"
    },
    {
     "n": 121,
     "text": "Exert themselves as if urgently trying to extinguish fires upon their heads.",
     "section": "Verse 28"
    },
    {
     "n": 122,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to cultivate concentration,",
     "section": "Verse 29"
    },
    {
     "n": 123,
     "text": "Which utterly transcends the four formless absorptions,",
     "section": "Verse 29"
    },
    {
     "n": 124,
     "text": "In the knowledge that mental afflictions are overcome entirely",
     "section": "Verse 29"
    },
    {
     "n": 125,
     "text": "Through penetrating insight suffused with stable calm.",
     "section": "Verse 29"
    },
    {
     "n": 126,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to cultivate wisdom,",
     "section": "Verse 30"
    },
    {
     "n": 127,
     "text": "Beyond the three conceptual spheres, alongside skilful means,",
     "section": "Verse 30"
    },
    {
     "n": 128,
     "text": "Since it is not possible to attain the perfect level of awakening",
     "section": "Verse 30"
    },
    {
     "n": 129,
     "text": "Through the other five pāramitās alone, in wisdom’s absence.",
     "section": "Verse 30"
    },
    {
     "n": 130,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to scrutinize oneself",
     "section": "Verse 31"
    },
    {
     "n": 131,
     "text": "Continually and to rid oneself of faults whenever they appear.",
     "section": "Verse 31"
    },
    {
     "n": 132,
     "text": "For unless one checks carefully to find one’s own confusion,",
     "section": "Verse 31"
    },
    {
     "n": 133,
     "text": "One might appear to be practising Dharma, but act against it.",
     "section": "Verse 31"
    },
    {
     "n": 134,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is never to speak ill",
     "section": "Verse 32"
    },
    {
     "n": 135,
     "text": "Of others who have embarked upon the greater vehicle,",
     "section": "Verse 32"
    },
    {
     "n": 136,
     "text": "For if, under the influence of destructive emotions,",
     "section": "Verse 32"
    },
    {
     "n": 137,
     "text": "I speak of other bodhisattvas’ failings, it is I who am at fault.",
     "section": "Verse 32"
    },
    {
     "n": 138,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to let go of attachment",
     "section": "Verse 33"
    },
    {
     "n": 139,
     "text": "To the households of benefactors and of family and friends,",
     "section": "Verse 33"
    },
    {
     "n": 140,
     "text": "Since one’s study, reflection and meditation will all diminish",
     "section": "Verse 33"
    },
    {
     "n": 141,
     "text": "When one quarrels and competes for honours and rewards.",
     "section": "Verse 33"
    },
    {
     "n": 142,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to avoid harsh words,",
     "section": "Verse 34"
    },
    {
     "n": 143,
     "text": "Which others might find unpleasant or distasteful,",
     "section": "Verse 34"
    },
    {
     "n": 144,
     "text": "Since abusive language upsets the minds of others,",
     "section": "Verse 34"
    },
    {
     "n": 145,
     "text": "And thereby undermines a bodhisattva’s conduct.",
     "section": "Verse 34"
    },
    {
     "n": 146,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to slay attachment",
     "section": "Verse 35"
    },
    {
     "n": 147,
     "text": "And the rest—mind’s afflictions—at once, the very moment they arise,",
     "section": "Verse 35"
    },
    {
     "n": 148,
     "text": "Taking as weapons the remedies held with mindfulness and vigilance.",
     "section": "Verse 35"
    },
    {
     "n": 149,
     "text": "For once the kleshas have become familiar, they’ll be harder to avert.",
     "section": "Verse 35"
    },
    {
     "n": 150,
     "text": "In short, no matter what one might be doing,",
     "section": "Verse 36"
    },
    {
     "n": 151,
     "text": "By examining always the status of one’s mind,",
     "section": "Verse 36"
    },
    {
     "n": 152,
     "text": "With continuous mindfulness and alertness,",
     "section": "Verse 36"
    },
    {
     "n": 153,
     "text": "To bring about the good of others—this is the practice of all the bodhisattvas.",
     "section": "Verse 36"
    },
    {
     "n": 154,
     "text": "The practice of all the bodhisattvas is to dedicate towards enlightenment",
     "section": "Verse 37"
    },
    {
     "n": 155,
     "text": "All the virtue to be gained through making effort in these ways,",
     "section": "Verse 37"
    },
    {
     "n": 156,
     "text": "With wisdom that is purified entirely of the three conceptual spheres,",
     "section": "Verse 37"
    },
    {
     "n": 157,
     "text": "So as to dispel the sufferings of the infinity of beings.",
     "section": "Verse 37"
    },
    {
     "n": 158,
     "text": "Here I have set down for those who wish to follow the bodhisattva path,"
    },
    {
     "n": 159,
     "text": "Thirty-seven practices to be adopted by all the buddhas’ heirs,"
    },
    {
     "n": 160,
     "text": "Based on what is taught in the sūtras, tantras and treatises,"
    },
    {
     "n": 161,
     "text": "And following the instructions of the great masters of the past."
    },
    {
     "n": 162,
     "text": "Since my intellect is only feeble and I have studied but a little,"
    },
    {
     "n": 163,
     "text": "This is not a composition likely to delight the connoisseurs,"
    },
    {
     "n": 164,
     "text": "Yet since I’ve relied upon the sūtras and what the saints have taught"
    },
    {
     "n": 165,
     "text": "I feel these are indeed the genuine trainings of the buddhas’ heirs."
    },
    {
     "n": 166,
     "text": "Still, the tremendous waves of activity of the bodhisattvas"
    },
    {
     "n": 167,
     "text": "Are difficult for simple-minded folk like me to comprehend,"
    },
    {
     "n": 168,
     "text": "And I must therefore beg the indulgence of all the perfect saints"
    },
    {
     "n": 169,
     "text": "For any contradictions, irrelevancies or other flaws this may contain."
    },
    {
     "n": 170,
     "text": "Through whatever merit has here been gained, may all beings"
    },
    {
     "n": 171,
     "text": "Generate sublime bodhicitta, both relative and absolute,"
    },
    {
     "n": 172,
     "text": "And through this, come to equal Lord Avalokiteśvara,"
    },
    {
     "n": 173,
     "text": "Transcending the extremes of existence and quiescence."
    },
    {
     "n": 174,
     "text": "This was composed in Jewel Cave (Rinchen Puk) in Ngulchu by the monk Tokme, a teacher of scripture and reasoning, for his own and others’ benefit."
    }
   ]
